# reading 2 of boethius-4.md by claude-opus-5-5
atom	bad_more_unfortunate	the bad are more unfortunate when they have accomplished their desires than if they are unable to get them fulfilled
atom	license_removed	that license which thou believest to be permitted to the wicked were taken away
atom	punishment_remitted	the punishment of the wicked would be in great part remitted
atom	will_evil_wretched	it is wretched to will evil
atom	able_more_wretched	to have been able to accomplish evil is more wretched than only to will it
atom	power_gives_effect	without the power the wretched will would fail of effect
atom	each_state_wretched	each one of these states (willing, being able to accomplish, accomplishing crime) has its own measure of wretchedness
atom	threefold	those who will, are able to accomplish, and accomplish crime are victims of a threefold wretchedness
# "needs must be" (S3) and "must needs" (S5) are read as marking inference, not metaphysical necessity, so no modal logic is used.
# S1 only says the matter will be shown later, so it is left out.
P1	S2	license_removed → punishment_remitted
P2	S3	bad_more_unfortunate
P3	S4	power_gives_effect
C1	S4	will_evil_wretched → able_more_wretched	from P3
P4	S5	each_state_wretched
C	S5	threefold	from C1 P4
